WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.188
The compliance track is for the people
who read evidence rather than build it:

2
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:09.362
ISSOs, compliance staff, assessors
and authorizing officials.

3
00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:12.188
It teaches one skill above all, tracing.

4
00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:16.631
Given a control, name the mechanism
that closes it, the book that built it,

5
00:00:16.631 --> 00:00:21.376
the record it emits, and where that
record sits in the authorization package.

6
00:00:21.376 --> 00:00:25.925
Given a record, work back to its control
and say whether it's still current.

7
00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:31.223
A foundations module covers the essentials,
like the Risk Management Framework,

8
00:00:31.223 --> 00:00:36.363
who owes which proof, and why Moderate and
FedRAMP's Class C are two facts, not one.

9
00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:41.050
Then the modules follow the program's evidence
areas, and each teaches a discipline.

10
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.506
For example, a policy
screenshot can't show a sign-in

11
00:00:44.506 --> 00:00:47.962
was phishing-resistant; only
the sign-in record can.

12
00:00:47.962 --> 00:00:51.949
The capstone is a continuous-monitoring
narrative for one system.

13
00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:53.640
Next, the builders.
